### Description

The Terraform program below configures a Route 53 hosted zone named "primary" and sets up AWS CloudWatch Logs to capture DNS query logs from this hosted zone. It includes creating a CloudWatch Log Group, a CloudWatch Log Stream, and a CloudWatch Log Resource Policy that allows Route 53 to put log events into the specified log group.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "zone_name" {
  description = "The name of the Route 53 hosted zone"
  default     = "example.com"
}

variable "log_group_name" {
  description = "The name of the CloudWatch Log Group"
  default     = "aws_route53_example_com"
}

variable "log_policy_name" {
  description = "The name of the CloudWatch Log Resource Policy"
  default     = "route53-query-logging-policy"
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "primary" {
  name = var.zone_name
}

resource "aws_cloudwatch_log_group" "route53_logs" {
  name              = var.log_group_name
  retention_in_days = 30  # Set the desired retention period
}

resource "aws_cloudwatch_log_stream" "route53_query_logs" {
  name           = "query-logs"
  log_group_name = aws_cloudwatch_log_group.route53_logs.name
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "route53_logging_role" {
  name = "route53-logging-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "route53.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_policy" "route53_logging_policy" {
  name        = var.log_policy_name
  description = "Policy allowing Route 53 to put logs into CloudWatch"

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "logs:CreateLogStream",
          "logs:PutLogEvents"
        ]
        Effect   = "Allow"
        Resource = aws_cloudwatch_log_group.route53_logs.arn
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "route53_logging_policy_attachment" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.route53_logging_role.name
  policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.route53_logging_policy.arn
}

resource "aws_route53_query_log" "primary" {
  hosted_zone_id = aws_route53_zone.primary.id
  cloudwatch_logs_log_group_arn = aws_cloudwatch_log_group.route53_logs.arn
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-east-1` region. You can change this to any other region as needed.

2. **Variables**: 
   - `zone_name`: The name of the Route 53 hosted zone.
   - `log_group_name`: The name of the CloudWatch Log Group.
   - `log_policy_name`: The name of the CloudWatch Log Resource Policy.

3. **Route 53 Hosted Zone**: A Route 53 hosted zone named "example.com" is created.

4. **CloudWatch Log Group and Stream**: A CloudWatch Log Group and a Log Stream are created to store the DNS query logs.

5. **IAM Role and Policy**: 
   - An IAM role (`route53-logging-role`) is created that Route 53 can assume.
   - An IAM policy (`route53-query-logging-policy`) is created to allow Route 53 to create log streams and put log events into the specified CloudWatch Log Group.
   - The policy is attached to the IAM role.

6. **Route 53 Query Log**: A Route 53 query log is configured to send DNS query logs to the specified CloudWatch Log Group.

This configuration ensures that DNS query logs for the "primary" hosted zone are captured and stored in CloudWatch Logs, with appropriate permissions set via IAM roles and policies.

