### Description

The Terraform program below creates a basic AWS CodeBuild project configured to use a GitHub repository as its source. It also sets up an IAM role with the necessary permissions for CodeBuild to access the repository and perform build actions.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "github_owner" {
  description = "The owner of the GitHub repository"
  type        = string
  default     = "your-github-username"
}

variable "github_repo" {
  description = "The name of the GitHub repository"
  type        = string
  default     = "your-repository-name"
}

variable "github_branch" {
  description = "The branch of the GitHub repository to build"
  type        = string
  default     = "main"
}

variable "project_name" {
  description = "The name of the CodeBuild project"
  type        = string
  default     = "example-codebuild-project"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "codebuild_role" {
  name = "${var.project_name}-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "codebuild.amazonaws.com"
        }
      },
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "codebuild_policy" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AWSCodeBuildDeveloperAccess"
  role       = aws_iam_role.codebuild_role.name
}

resource "aws_codebuild_project" "example" {
  name         = var.project_name
  service_role = aws_iam_role.codebuild_role.arn

  source {
    type            = "GITHUB"
    location        = "https://github.com/${var.github_owner}/${var.github_repo}.git"
    git_clone_depth = 1
    buildspec       = file("buildspec.yml")
  }

  artifacts {
    type = "NO_ARTIFACTS"
  }

  environment {
    compute_type                = "BUILD_GENERAL1_SMALL"
    image                       = "aws/codebuild/standard:6.0"
    type                        = "LINUX_CONTAINER"
    image_pull_credentials_type = "CODEBUILD"
  }
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-east-1` region.
2. **Variables**: Several variables are defined to allow customization of the GitHub repository details and the CodeBuild project name.
3. **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `${var.project_name}-role` is created with a trust policy allowing CodeBuild to assume it.
4. **IAM Role Policy Attachment**: The `AWSCodeBuildDeveloperAccess` policy is attached to the IAM role to grant the necessary permissions.
5. **CodeBuild Project**: A CodeBuild project is created with the specified name and IAM role. The source is configured to use a GitHub repository, and the buildspec file is assumed to be located in the root of the repository. No artifacts are generated by this project.

This configuration can be deployed using Terraform version `~> 1.9.8` and the AWS provider version `~> 5.75`. Make sure to replace the default values of the variables with your actual GitHub repository details and desired project name.

