### Description

The Terraform program below defines a Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream configured to deliver data to an S3 bucket with dynamic partitioning enabled. The program includes necessary IAM roles and policies to ensure proper permissions for the Firehose delivery stream to access the S3 bucket.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

variable "firehose_name" {
  description = "The name of the Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream"
  type        = string
  default     = "my-firehose-stream"
}

variable "s3_bucket_name" {
  description = "The name of the S3 bucket where data will be delivered"
  type        = string
  default     = "my-s3-bucket"
}

variable "s3_prefix" {
  description = "The prefix for the S3 object keys"
  type        = string
  default     = "firehose-data/"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "firehose_bucket" {
  bucket = var.s3_bucket_name
  acl    = "private"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "firehose_role" {
  name = "${var.firehose_name}-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "firehose.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "firehose_policy" {
  name = "${var.firehose_name}-policy"
  role = aws_iam_role.firehose_role.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "s3:AbortMultipartUpload",
          "s3:GetBucketLocation",
          "s3:ListBucket",
          "s3:ListBucketMultipartUploads",
          "s3:PutObject"
        ]
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = [
          aws_s3_bucket.firehose_bucket.arn,
          "${aws_s3_bucket.firehose_bucket.arn}/*"
        ]
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream" "firehose_stream" {
  name        = var.firehose_name
  destination = "s3"

  s3_configuration {
    role_arn       = aws_iam_role.firehose_role.arn
    bucket_arn     = aws_s3_bucket.firehose_bucket.arn
    prefix         = var.s3_prefix
    buffering_hints {
      size_in_mbs = 6
      interval_in_seconds = 300
    }
    compression_format = "UNCOMPRESSED"
    dynamic_partitioning_configuration {
      enabled = true
      retry_options {
        duration_in_seconds = 300
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **Variables**: 
   - `firehose_name`: The name of the Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream.
   - `s3_bucket_name`: The name of the S3 bucket where data will be delivered.
   - `s3_prefix`: The prefix for the S3 object keys.
3. **S3 Bucket**: An S3 bucket is created to store the data delivered by the Firehose.
4. **IAM Role and Policy**: 
   - An IAM role is created for the Firehose to assume.
   - An IAM policy is attached to the role allowing it to perform necessary actions on the S3 bucket.
5. **Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream**: 
   - A Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream is created with an S3 destination.
   - Dynamic partitioning is enabled with specified retry options.

This configuration ensures that the Firehose can deliver data to the specified S3 bucket with dynamic partitioning enabled, and all necessary permissions are in place.

