### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = var.region
}

variable "region" {
  description = "The AWS region to deploy the resources"
  type        = string
  default     = "us-east-1"
}

variable "firehose_name" {
  description = "The name of the Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream"
  type        = string
  default     = "newrelic-firehose-stream"
}

variable "http_endpoint_url" {
  description = "The URL of the HTTP endpoint (e.g., New Relic)"
  type        = string
  default     = "https://example.com/newrelic"
}

variable "role_name" {
  description = "The name of the IAM role for Kinesis Firehose"
  type        = string
  default     = "KinesisFirehoseToHTTPRole"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "firehose_role" {
  name = var.role_name

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "firehose.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "firehose_policy" {
  name = "${var.role_name}-policy"
  role = aws_iam_role.firehose_role.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "logs:CreateLogGroup",
          "logs:CreateLogStream",
          "logs:PutLogEvents"
        ]
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = "*"
      },
      {
        Action = "ec2:DescribeVpcs",
        Effect = "Allow",
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream" "firehose_stream" {
  name        = var.firehose_name
  destination = "http_endpoint"

  http_endpoint_configuration {
    url = var.http_endpoint_url

    buffering_hints {
      size_in_mbs       = 6
      interval_in_seconds = 300
    }

    request_configuration {
      content_encoding = "NONE"
    }

    s3_configuration {
      role_arn         = aws_iam_role.firehose_role.arn
      bucket_arn       = "arn:aws:s3:::your-s3-bucket-name"
      prefix           = "firehose/"
      buffering_hints {
        size_in_mbs       = 6
        interval_in_seconds = 300
      }
      compression_format = "UNCOMPRESSED"
    }

    cloudwatch_logging_options {
      enabled         = true
      log_group_name  = "/aws/kinesisfirehose/${var.firehose_name}"
      log_stream_name = "DeliveryToHTTP"
    }
  }

  tags = {
    Name = var.firehose_name
  }
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a default region (`us-east-1`), which can be overridden using the `region` variable.

2. **Variables**: Several variables are defined to make the configuration flexible:
   - `region`: The AWS region where the resources will be deployed.
   - `firehose_name`: The name of the Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream.
   - `http_endpoint_url`: The URL of the HTTP endpoint (e.g., New Relic).
   - `role_name`: The name of the IAM role for Kinesis Firehose.

3. **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `KinesisFirehoseToHTTPRole` is created, allowing Kinesis Firehose to assume the role.

4. **IAM Role Policy**: A policy is attached to the IAM role, granting permissions for logging and describing VPCs.

5. **Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream**: The delivery stream is configured to send data to an HTTP endpoint:
   - `buffering_hints`: Configures the buffer size and interval.
   - `request_configuration`: Specifies the content encoding.
   - `s3_configuration`: Configures an S3 bucket for backup and error logging.
   - `cloudwatch_logging_options`: Enables logging to CloudWatch.

6. **Tags**: Tags are added to the delivery stream for easy identification.

This configuration ensures that the Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream is properly set up to deliver data to the specified HTTP endpoint while adhering to best practices for security and logging.

