### Description

The Terraform script provided below will configure an OpenID Connect (OIDC) identity provider for an AWS EKS cluster named "example". The script includes the necessary resources to create the OIDC provider and link it to the EKS cluster. It also defines variables with default values to ensure flexibility and reusability.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "eks_cluster_name" {
  description = "The name of the EKS cluster"
  default     = "example"
}

variable "oidc_provider_config_name" {
  description = "The name of the OIDC provider configuration"
  default     = "example-oidc-provider"
}

variable "oidc_issuer_url" {
  description = "The issuer URL of the OIDC provider"
  default     = "https://example.com"
}

variable "oidc_client_id" {
  description = "The client ID of the OIDC provider"
  default     = "example-client-id"
}

resource "aws_iam_openid_connect_provider" "oidc_provider" {
  url             = var.oidc_issuer_url
  client_id_list  = [var.oidc_client_id]
  thumbprint_list = ["<thumbprint>"]  # Replace with the actual thumbprint of the issuer certificate
}

resource "aws_eks_identity_provider_config" "oidc_identity_provider" {
  name         = var.oidc_provider_config_name
  cluster_name = var.eks_cluster_name

  oidc {
    client_id     = var.oidc_client_id
    groups_claim  = "groups"
    identity_provider_config_name = var.oidc_provider_config_name
    issuer        = var.oidc_issuer_url
    required_claims = {}
  }
}
```

### Notes:
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a default region (`us-west-2`). You can change this to your preferred region.
2. **Variables**: Default values are provided for the EKS cluster name, OIDC provider configuration name, issuer URL, and client ID. These can be overridden when applying the Terraform configuration.
3. **Thumbprint**: The `thumbprint_list` in the `aws_iam_openid_connect_provider` resource requires the thumbprint of the issuer certificate. You need to replace `<thumbprint>` with the actual thumbprint value.
4. **IAM Role**: The script assumes that the necessary IAM roles and permissions are already set up to allow the creation of the OIDC provider and linking it to the EKS cluster.

