The Terraform program below creates an AWS Lambda function and sets up a CloudWatch Event Rule to trigger the Lambda function every 15 minutes. The Lambda function is written in Python and logs a simple message to CloudWatch Logs. The necessary IAM roles and policies are also created to allow the Lambda function to execute and the CloudWatch Event Rule to trigger it.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

variable "lambda_function_name" {
  description = "The name of the Lambda function"
