### Description

The Terraform program defined below sets up an AWS CloudFront distribution to serve content from an S3 bucket. It includes:

1. **AWS CloudFront Distribution**: Configured with an origin pointing to an S3 bucket, using a CloudFront Origin Access Control (OAC) for secure access. The distribution allows only GET and HEAD methods, caches these methods, and uses a default cache behavior with an "allow-all" viewer protocol policy. It is priced at the "PriceClass_200" level and restricts access to specific geographic locations (US, CA, GB, DE). The distribution uses the CloudFront default SSL certificate.

2. **AWS Route53 Zone**: Creates a Route53 hosted zone for the domain "netflix.com".

3. **AWS Route53 Record Resources**: Two DNS records are created within the Route53 hosted zone, linking to the CloudFront distribution.

4. **CloudFront Origin Access Control**: Sets up an OAC to allow CloudFront to access the S3 bucket securely.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "s3_bucket_name" {
  description = "The name of the S3 bucket to use as the origin."
  type        = string
}

variable "cloudfront_distribution_name" {
  description = "The name of the CloudFront distribution."
  type        = string
  default     = "my-video-content-distribution"
}

variable "route53_zone_name" {
  description = "The name of the Route53 zone."
  type        = string
  default     = "netflix.com"
}

variable "route53_record_names" {
  description = "The names of the Route53 records."
  type        = list(string)
  default     = ["www", "video"]
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "video_content" {
  bucket = var.s3_bucket_name
  acl    = "private"
}

resource "aws_cloudfront_origin_access_control" "oac" {
  name                              = "${var.cloudfront_distribution_name}-oac"
  origin_access_control_origin_type = "s3"
  signing_behavior                  = "always"
  signing_protocol                  = "sigv4"
}

resource "aws_cloudfront_distribution" "video_content_distribution" {
  origin {
    domain_name              = "${aws_s3_bucket.video_content.bucket_regional_domain_name}"
    origin_access_control_id = aws_cloudfront_origin_access_control.oac.id
    origin_id                = "s3_video_content_origin"
  }

  default_cache_behavior {
    allowed_methods  = ["GET", "HEAD"]
    cached_methods   = ["GET", "HEAD"]
    target_origin_id = "s3_video_content_origin"
    viewer_protocol_policy = "allow-all"
  }

  price_class = "PriceClass_200"

  restrictions {
    geo_restriction {
      restriction_type = "whitelist"
      locations        = ["US", "CA", "GB", "DE"]
    }
  }

  viewer_certificate {
    cloudfront_default_certificate = true
  }
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "netflix_com" {
  name = var.route53_zone_name
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "route53_records" {
  count = length(var.route53_record_names)

  zone_id = aws_route53_zone.netflix_com.zone_id
  name    = "${element(var.route53_record_names, count.index)}.${var.route53_zone_name}"
  type    = "A"
  ttl     = 300

  aliases {
    name                   = aws_cloudfront_distribution.video_content_distribution.domain_name
    zone_id                = aws_cloudfront_distribution.video_content_distribution.hosted_zone_id
    evaluate_target_health = false
  }
}
```

### Explanation

- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-east-1` region.
- **Variables**: Several variables are defined to allow customization of the S3 bucket name, CloudFront distribution name, Route53 zone name, and Route53 record names.
- **S3 Bucket**: An S3 bucket is created and set to private.
- **CloudFront Origin Access Control**: An OAC is created to allow CloudFront to access the S3 bucket.
- **CloudFront Distribution**: A CloudFront distribution is set up with the specified origin, cache behavior, pricing class, geographic restrictions, and SSL certificate.
- **Route53 Zone**: A Route53 hosted zone is created for the domain "netflix.com".
- **Route53 Records**: Two DNS records are created within the Route53 hosted zone, linking to the CloudFront distribution.

This configuration ensures that the CloudFront distribution is properly set up to serve content from the S3 bucket, while the Route53 records ensure that the domain "netflix.com" points to the CloudFront distribution.

