### Description

The Terraform program below sets up a PostgreSQL 15 instance on AWS RDS within specific public subnets. This setup is intended for running Airbyte connector test cases. The RDS instance uses managed settings to minimize maintenance overhead. The allocated storage is set to 5 GB, and the instance type is "db.t3.micro". Additionally, necessary IAM roles and policies are created to ensure proper access control.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "vpc_id" {
  description = "The ID of the VPC where the RDS instance will be deployed"
  type        = string
}

variable "public_subnet_ids" {
  description = "A list of public subnet IDs where the RDS instance will be placed"
  type        = list(string)
}

variable "db_name" {
  description = "The name of the database"
  type        = string
  default     = "airbyte_test_db"
}

variable "db_username" {
  description = "The username for the database"
  type        = string
  default     = "airbyte_user"
}

variable "db_password" {
  description = "The password for the database user"
  type        = string
  sensitive   = true
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "rds_access_role" {
  name = "rds-access-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "rds.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "rds_access_policy" {
  name = "rds-access-policy"
  role = aws_iam_role.rds_access_role.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "ec2:Describe*",
          "ec2:Connect"
        ]
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_rds_instance" "airbyte_postgres" {
  identifier              = "airbyte-postgres-instance"
  engine                  = "postgres"
  engine_version          = "15"
  instance_class          = "db.t3.micro"
  allocated_storage       = 5
  db_name                 = var.db_name
  username                = var.db_username
  password                = var.db_password
  vpc_security_group_ids  = [aws_security_group.rds_sg.id]
  db_subnet_group_name    = aws_db_subnet_group.rds_subnet_group.name
  publicly_accessible     = true
  skip_final_snapshot     = true
  iam_database_authentication_enabled = true
  deletion_protection     = false
}

resource "aws_security_group" "rds_sg" {
  name        = "airbyte-rds-sg"
  description = "Security group for Airbyte RDS instance"
  vpc_id      = var.vpc_id

  ingress {
    from_port   = 5432
    to_port     = 5432
    protocol    = "tcp"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]  # Adjust this to restrict access if needed
  }

  egress {
    from_port   = 0
    to_port     = 0
    protocol    = "-1"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }
}

resource "aws_db_subnet_group" "rds_subnet_group" {
  name       = "airbyte-rds-subnet-group"
  subnet_ids = var.public_subnet_ids

  tags = {
    Name = "Airbyte RDS Subnet Group"
  }
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a specific region (`us-west-2`).

2. **Variables**: Several variables are defined to allow customization of the RDS instance, such as the VPC ID, public subnet IDs, database name, username, and password.

3. **IAM Role and Policy**: An IAM role (`rds_access_role`) and policy (`rds_access_policy`) are created to allow the RDS instance to perform necessary actions.

4. **RDS Instance**: The `aws_rds_instance` resource creates a PostgreSQL 15 instance with the specified parameters, including the instance class, allocated storage, and security group.

5. **Security Group**: A security group (`rds_sg`) is created to allow inbound traffic on port 5432 (PostgreSQL) from any IP address. Adjust the CIDR block as needed for security.

6. **DB Subnet Group**: A DB subnet group (`rds_subnet_group`) is created to specify the subnets where the RDS instance will be deployed.

This configuration ensures that the RDS instance is properly set up for running Airbyte connector test cases with minimal maintenance.

