### Description

This Terraform program will create a basic Amazon Lightsail instance. The configuration includes setting up the necessary AWS provider, creating an IAM role with the required permissions for Lightsail, and deploying a Lightsail instance with default settings. The instance will use a predefined blueprint and bundle, and it will be launched in a specified AWS region.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = var.region
}

variable "region" {
  description = "The AWS region to deploy the Lightsail instance"
  type        = string
  default     = "us-east-1"
}

variable "instance_name" {
  description = "The name of the Lightsail instance"
  type        = string
  default     = "my-lightsail-instance"
}

variable "blueprint_id" {
  description = "The ID of the Lightsail blueprint"
  type        = string
  default     = "ubuntu_20_04"
}

variable "bundle_id" {
  description = "The ID of the Lightsail bundle"
  type        = string
  default     = "nano_1_0"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "lightsail_role" {
  name = "LightsailInstanceRole"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "lightsail.amazonaws.com"
        }
      },
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "lightsail_policy" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonLightsailFullAccess"
  role       = aws_iam_role.lightsail_role.name
}

resource "aws_lightsail_instance" "example" {
  name              = var.instance_name
  availability_zone = data.aws_availability_zones.available.names[0]
  blueprint_id      = var.blueprint_id
  bundle_id         = var.bundle_id
  key_pair_name     = var.key_pair_name
  tags = {
    Name = var.instance_name
  }
}

data "aws_availability_zones" "available" {
  state = "available"
}
```

### Notes

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a default region (`us-east-1`), which can be overridden using the `region` variable.
2. **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `LightsailInstanceRole` is created with the necessary permissions to manage Lightsail instances.
3. **Lightsail Instance**: A Lightsail instance is created with the specified name, blueprint, and bundle. The instance is launched in the first available availability zone.
4. **Variables**: Default values are provided for the region, instance name, blueprint ID, and bundle ID. You can override these defaults when applying the Terraform configuration.
5. **Key Pair**: The `key_pair_name` variable is not defined in the provided configuration. Ensure you have a key pair created in AWS and provide its name when applying the configuration.

To deploy this configuration, ensure you have the necessary AWS credentials configured and run `terraform init`, `terraform plan`, and `terraform apply`.

