2. **IAM Role**: Creates an IAM role with permissions to access the S3 Glacier vault and publish messages to SNS.
3. **S3 Glacier Vault**: Creates an S3 Glacier vault.
4. **SNS Topic**: Creates an SNS topic for notifications.
5. **SNS Subscription**: Subscribes an email address to the SNS topic.
6. **S3 Glacier Vault Notification Configuration**: Configures the S3 Glacier vault to send notifications to the SNS topic.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = var.region
}

variable "region" {
  description = "The AWS region to deploy the resources"
  type        = string
  default     = "us-west-2"
}

variable "vault_name" {
  description = "The name of the S3 Glacier vault"
  type        = string
  default     = "my-glacier-vault"
}

variable "sns_topic_name" {
  description = "The name of the SNS topic"
  type        = string
  default     = "glacier-notifications"
}

variable "sns_email_subscriber" {
  description = "The email address to subscribe to the SNS topic"
  type        = string
  default     = "example@example.com"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "glacier_sns_role" {
  name = "GlacierSNSTopicRole"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "glacier.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_policy" "glacier_sns_policy" {
  name        = "GlacierSNSTopicPolicy"
  description = "Policy to allow Glacier to publish to SNS"

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "sns:Publish"
        ]
        Effect   = "Allow"
        Resource = aws_sns_topic.glacier_notifications.arn
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "glacier_sns_policy_attachment" {
  policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.glacier_sns_policy.arn
  role       = aws_iam_role.glacier_sns_role.name
}

resource "aws_s3_glacier_vault" "my_vault" {
  name = var.vault_name
}

resource "aws_sns_topic" "glacier_notifications" {
  name = var.sns_topic_name
}

resource "aws_sns_topic_subscription" "email_subscription" {
  topic_arn = aws_sns_topic.glacier_notifications.arn
  protocol  = "email"
  endpoint  = var.sns_email_subscriber
}

resource "aws_s3_glacier_vault_notifications" "vault_notifications" {
  vault_name = aws_s3_glacier_vault.my_vault.name

  events = [
    "ArchiveRetrievalCompleted",
    "InventoryRetrievalCompleted",
    "JobCompleted",
    "JobFailed"
  ]

  sns_topic = aws_sns_topic.glacier_notifications.arn
}
```

### Explanation

- **Provider Configuration**: The `aws` provider is configured with a default region (`us-west-2`), which can be overridden using the `region` variable.
- **IAM Role and Policy**: An IAM role (`GlacierSNSTopicRole`) is created with a trust policy allowing Glacier to assume the role. An IAM policy (`GlacierSNSTopicPolicy`) grants permission to publish messages to the SNS topic. The policy is attached to the IAM role.
- **S3 Glacier Vault**: An S3 Glacier vault (`my-glacier-vault`) is created.
- **SNS Topic and Subscription**: An SNS topic (`glacier-notifications`) is created, and an email subscription is added to the topic.
- **Vault Notifications**: The S3 Glacier vault is configured to send notifications for specific events (e.g., job completion, retrieval completion) to the SNS topic.

This Terraform configuration ensures that the S3 Glacier vault is properly set up with notifications sent to an SNS topic, which can then be subscribed to by email or other endpoints.

