### Description

The Terraform program below defines an AWS S3 Glacier vault along with an access policy that controls who can perform actions on the vault. The configuration includes:

- **Provider Configuration**: Sets up the AWS provider with a specific region.
- **S3 Glacier Vault Resource**: Creates an S3 Glacier vault.
- **IAM Policy Resource**: Defines an IAM policy that specifies permissions for accessing the S3 Glacier vault.
- **IAM Role Resource**: Creates an IAM role that attaches the defined policy.
- **IAM Role Policy Attachment Resource**: Attaches the IAM policy to the IAM role.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "vault_name" {
  description = "The name of the S3 Glacier vault"
  type        = string
  default     = "my-glacier-vault"
}

variable "policy_arn" {
  description = "ARN of the IAM policy to attach to the role"
  type        = string
  default     = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonGlacierReadOnlyAccess"
}

resource "aws_s3_glacier_vault" "example" {
  name = var.vault_name
}

resource "aws_iam_policy" "glacier_access_policy" {
  name        = "GlacierVaultAccessPolicy"
  description = "Policy to allow access to the S3 Glacier vault"

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect   = "Allow",
        Action   = [
          "glacier:ListJobs",
          "glacier:DescribeJob",
          "glacier:GetJobOutput",
          "glacier:InitiateJob",
          "glacier:UploadArchive",
          "glacier:InventoryRetrieval"
        ],
        Resource = aws_s3_glacier_vault.example.arn
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "glacier_access_role" {
  name = "GlacierAccessRole"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole",
        Effect = "Allow",
        Principal = {
          Service = "ec2.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "attach_glacier_policy" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.glacier_access_role.name
  policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.glacier_access_policy.arn
}
```

### Explanation

- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region. You can change this to any other region as needed.
- **Variables**:
  - `vault_name`: The name of the S3 Glacier vault. It defaults to `"my-glacier-vault"`.
  - `policy_arn`: The ARN of the IAM policy to attach to the role. It defaults to `"arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonGlacierReadOnlyAccess"`, but you can customize it to fit your needs.
- **Resources**:
  - `aws_s3_glacier_vault`: Creates an S3 Glacier vault with the specified name.
  - `aws_iam_policy`: Defines an IAM policy that allows various actions on the S3 Glacier vault.
  - `aws_iam_role`: Creates an IAM role that can assume the policy.
  - `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment`: Attaches the IAM policy to the IAM role.

This configuration ensures that the S3 Glacier vault is created and secured with the appropriate access policies.

